DEEP PATTERN ANALYSIS — FOUR CATEGORIES THROUGH n=7
oracle-2026-05-11
========================================================

KEY THEOREM (proved this session):
  Grid-symmetry ↔ Self-complementarity
  
  A tiling M is grid-symmetric iff T(M) is a SC tournament (iso class).
  
  Proof sketch:
  - TRANS_MAP τ on tilings corresponds to T → (T^op)^σ_n on tournaments
    (where σ_n(v)=n+1-v is vertex-label reversal)
  - SC class: τ maps C to itself → involution on odd-sized set → ≥1 fixed point
  - NS class: τ maps C to C^op ≠ C → no fixed points in C
  - bl(C) = #fixed points = odd positive integer for SC, 0 for NS
  
  Consequence: 2^{free_bits} grid-sym tilings distributed EXCLUSIVELY among SC classes,
  each receiving a positive odd number. NS classes get zero.

